he manuscript name ‘ Lygus yapensis ’ handwritten by Carvalho (Fig. 58). Using the species key in CARVALHO (1956, p. 83) the pale apex of antennal segment II, dark apical cuneal mark, uniformly dark pronotum, mostly dark dorsum, and tibial spines without dark basal spots allows us to determine the latter male as L. dybasi Carvalho, 1956. The male genitalia (Figs 144 – 146) also matches the illustrations in CARVALHO (1956, figs 50 e – g) for this species. However the collecting information “ Babeldaob: Ngarard 17. viii. 1939 Teiso Esaki ” is not among the paratypes listed in the original description of L. dybasi.","","text","",""]]},"RNGPN":{"d":[["CK","CK","iso","",""]]},"RQYCF":{"d":[["Norway","NO","iso","",""]]},"RTYF":{"d":[["Afrotropical(Namibia, Republic South Africa:North West Province, Zimbabwe)","","text","",""]]},"RWKMD":{"d":[["North America","","text","",""]]},"S3YF":{"d":[["South African Coast","50353","mrgid","",""]]},"SFRZ":{"d":[["Europe & Northern Asia (excluding China)","","text","",""]]},"SG29":{"d":[["Africa","","text","",""]]},"SXFPD":{"d":[["ZA, Eastern Cape","","text","native",""],["ZA, Western Cape","","text","native",""]]},"SYLM":{"d":[["Slovenia","48523","mrgid","",""]]},"T73VQ":{"d":[["Distribution. Indonesia: Sumatra; Malaysia: Borneo (Sabah). It is reported for the first time from Borneo.","","text","",""]]},"TRWH":{"d":[["","CL","iso","native",""],["Chile","","text","native",""]]},"TWRVR":{"d":[["","VIE","tdwg","",""]]},"V37S2":{"d":[["Distribution. Thailand (Buengkan Province).","","text","",""]]},"V7FHJ":{"d":[["Denmark","48122","mrgid","",""]]},"VBWDR":{"d":[["","CO","iso","",""]]},"X4HQ":{"d":[["Brazil","","text","native",""]]},"YSFS":{"d":[["","BUL-OO","tdwg","native",""],["","YUG-CR","tdwg","native",""],["Bulgaria, Croatia","","text","native",""]]},"YSG2":{"d":[["","AUT-AU","tdwg","native",""],["","FRA-FR","tdwg","native",""],["","ITA-IT","tdwg","native",""],["","SWI-OO","tdwg","native",""],["France, Switzerland, Austria, Italy",""